  - *Objectives Resolution (13 Dec 1946):* Moved by Jawaharlal Nehru; adopted unanimously on 22 January 1947; formed the conceptual basis of the Preamble.
  - *Abolition of Separate Electorates:* Patel called it "a poison in the body politic"; Pant warned against minority isolation; Begum Aizaz Rasul supported abolition.
  - *Tribal Democracy Champion:* Jaipal Singh proclaimed: "You cannot teach democracy to the tribal people; you have to learn democracy from them."
  - *Santhanam's Federal Warning:* K. Santhanam warned that fiscal centralization would reduce states to "beggars" knocking on the Centre's door.
  - *The Language Compromise:* The Munshi-Ayyangar Formula made Hindi the *Official Language* (not National Language) and retained English for 15 years.
  - *Adoption vs Commencement Dates:* Adopted on *26 November 1949*; commenced on *26 January 1950* (to honor 1930 Purna Swaraj Day).
  - *Ambedkar's Farewell Address (25 Nov 1949):* Warned against entering a "life of contradictions"—political equality alongside social-economic inequality.
]

