#cheatsheet-box(title: "MASTER STRATEGY CHEATSHEET — THE MAKING OF THE CONSTITUTION")[
  ▸*Assembly Composition:* Formed under 1946 Cabinet Mission Plan; indirect elections; 300 members post-Partition; 82% Congress; Dr. Rajendra Prasad (President); Dr. B.R. Ambedkar (Drafting Committee Chair); B.N. Rau (Advisor); S.N. Mukherjee (Chief Draughtsman).
  ▸*Objectives Resolution (1946):* Defined India as an "Independent Sovereign Republic"; synthesized ideals of American, French, and Russian revolutions; enacted Universal Adult Franchise (Article 326).
  ▸*Debates on Rights & Castes:* Separate electorates abolished post-Partition; Article 17 abolished untouchability; reservations introduced for SCs and STs; Fifth & Sixth Schedules for tribal self-governance.
  ▸*Federal Distribution:* Union List (97 subjects), State List (66), Concurrent List (47); residuary powers with the Union (Article 248); Article 356 (President's Rule); fiscal centralization critiqued by K. Santhanam.
  ▸*Language Settlement:* R.V. Dhulekar's militant advocacy for Hindi opposed by G. Durgabai and Shankarrao Deo; Munshi-Ayyangar formula adopted Hindi as Official Language and preserved English for 15 years.
  ▸*Commencement:* Signed by 284 members on 26 Nov 1949; enacted on 26 Jan 1950; Ambedkar warned of danger if social-economic inequality remained unaddressed.
]

#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Trap 1 (Assembly Election Mechanism):* Assuming members were directly elected by universal suffrage. Members were *indirectly elected* by provincial legislative assemblies under restricted franchise.
  2. *Trap 2 (Constitutional Roles Attribution):* Confusing Drafting Chair with Constitutional Advisor. *Dr. B.R. Ambedkar* was Drafting Committee Chair; *B.N. Rau* was Constitutional Advisor.
  3. *Trap 3 (Separate Electorates Outcome):* Assuming separate electorates were retained for Scheduled Castes. Separate electorates were *completely abolished*; SCs/STs received *reserved seats* in joint electorates.
  4. *Trap 4 (Hindi as National Language):* Believing Hindi was designated the "National Language". The Constitution designated Hindi as the *Official Language of the Union*, NOT the National Language!
  5. *Trap 5 (English Retention Period):* The Munshi-Ayyangar formula retained English for *15 years* (until 1965), NOT permanently or for 5 years.
  6. *Trap 6 (Adoption vs Commencement Date):* Confusing 26 November 1949 (Constitution Day, Adoption) with 26 January 1950 (Republic Day, Commencement).
  7. *Trap 7 (Residuary Powers Jurisdiction):* Assuming residuary powers belong to the States as in the US. In India, residuary powers belong exclusively to the *Union Parliament* (Article 248).
]

