#mcq(3, [Under the constitutional framework formulated by the British Cabinet Mission Plan of 1946, members of the Constituent Assembly were:], (
  [Indirectly elected by the members of the Provincial Legislative Assemblies],
  [Directly elected by all Indian citizens on the basis of universal adult franchise],
  [Nominated exclusively by the Governor-General in Council],
  [Appointed directly by the British Parliament in London],
))
#solution(3, [Election Mode of the Assembly:
- Members of the Constituent Assembly were *indirectly elected* by the newly elected Provincial Legislative Assemblies.
- Seats were allocated to provinces and princely states in proportion to their respective populations (roughly 1 to 1 million).
Therefore, Option A is the correct answer.], answer: [A])

#mcq(4, [Who served as the Chairman of the Drafting Committee of the Constituent Assembly, playing the preeminent role in structuring the Indian Constitution?], (
  [Jawaharlal Nehru],
  [Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel],
  [Dr. Rajendra Prasad],
  [Dr. B.R. Ambedkar],
))
#solution(4, [Chairman of the Drafting Committee:
- *Dr. B.R. Ambedkar* served as Chairman of the *Drafting Committee*.
- Famed for his unmatched legal learning and commitment to social emancipation, he is celebrated as the "Father of the Indian Constitution".
Therefore, Option D is the correct answer.], answer: [D])

#mcq(5, [Which eminent jurist served as the Constitutional Advisor to the Government of India, preparing comprehensive background reports and initial comparative drafts?], (
  [B.N. Rau],
  [S.N. Mukherjee],
  [Alladi Krishnaswami Ayyar],
  [K.M. Munshi],
))
#solution(5, [Constitutional Advisor B.N. Rau:
- *Sir B.N. Rau* served as the *Constitutional Advisor*.
- He surveyed international democratic constitutions across the world, preparing comparative papers and the initial basic draft of the Constitution.
Therefore, Option A is the correct answer.], answer: [A])

