== Part 3: Adoption, Enactment, Adult Franchise & Warnings (Q11 to Q15)

#mcq(11, [On which date did the Constituent Assembly of India formally adopt, enact, and give to themselves the Constitution of India?], (
  [15 August 1947],
  [26 January 1950],
  [26 November 1949],
  [22 January 1947],
))
#solution(11, [Adoption Date of the Constitution:
- The Constitution was formally adopted and enacted on *26 November 1949* (now celebrated as Constitution Day).
- It came into full legal commencement on *26 January 1950* to commemorate the 1930 Purna Swaraj Day.
Therefore, Option C is the correct answer.], answer: [C])

#mcq(12, [Who served as the brilliant Chief Draughtsman of the Constituent Assembly, whose unmatched talent for phrasing intricate proposals into precise legal language was praised by Ambedkar?], (
  [S.N. Mukherjee],
  [B.N. Rau],
  [Sachchidananda Sinha],
  [H.V.R. Iengar],
))
#solution(12, [S.N. Mukherjee as Chief Draughtsman:
- *S.N. Mukherjee* served as the *Chief Draughtsman*.
- In his final address, Dr. Ambedkar showered high praise on Mukherjee for his exceptional ability to draft complex political compromises into clear statutory language.
Therefore, Option A is the correct answer.], answer: [A])

#mcq(13, [In his historic farewell address to the Constituent Assembly on 25 November 1949, Dr. B.R. Ambedkar warned that political democracy would be imperiled unless accompanied by:], (
  [The mandatory conscription of all citizens into the armed forces],
  [The immediate nationalization of all private agricultural lands],
  [A total prohibition on the formation of regional political parties],
  [Social and economic equality (fraternity) in the daily lives of citizens],
))
#solution(13, [Ambedkar's Farewell Warning:
- On *25 November 1949*, Dr. Ambedkar warned that India was entering a *"life of contradictions"*—political equality alongside social and economic inequality.
- He warned that unless social and economic democracy was achieved, those suffering inequality would blow up political democracy.
Therefore, Option D is the correct answer.], answer: [D])

#mcq(14, [Under Article 326 of the Constitution of India, Universal Adult Franchise was adopted granting voting rights to all adult citizens without which colonial disqualifications?], (
  [Gender qualifications only],
  [Property, taxation, educational, and gender qualifications],
  [Age and mental soundness requirements],
  [Citizenship and residence requirements],
))
#solution(14, [Universal Adult Franchise (Article 326):
- Article 326 established *Universal Adult Franchise*, completely abolishing British colonial restrictions based on property ownership, tax payments, educational degrees, or gender.
Therefore, Option B is the correct answer.], answer: [B])

#mcq(15, [Who served as the permanent President of the Constituent Assembly, steering its intense debates with patience, dignity, and consensus from December 1946 to January 1950?], (
  [Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel],
  [Jawaharlal Nehru],
  [Dr. Rajendra Prasad],
  [Dr. B.R. Ambedkar],
))
#solution(15, [President of the Constituent Assembly:
- *Dr. Rajendra Prasad* was elected permanent President of the Constituent Assembly on 11 December 1946.
- He guided all proceedings and was later elected the first President of the Republic of India.
Therefore, Option C is the correct answer.], answer: [C])
